course: dictionary
lesson: 5568
title: Less: smaller, not so much, or minus
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Less usually means a smaller amount. «Breathed-out air contains less oxygen and more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.» Less oxygen means a smaller amount of oxygen, not no oxygen at all.
explain: Less can also mean not so much. «Asking what will happen first makes it less strange.» The strangeness is not gone, just not as strong. Least means the smallest amount of all.
explain: In maths, less compares two amounts or takes away. «5 is less than 8» means 5 is the smaller number, written 5 < 8. «Ten less two is eight» uses less to mean minus. Read the words around less to decide which meaning it has.
fact: Less means a smaller amount, or not so much.
fact: «Less than» compares two amounts: 5 is less than 8 (5 < 8).
fact: In sums, «ten less two is eight» means ten minus two.
fact: Least means the smallest amount of all.
fact: The sign < means «less than», and its point is on the smaller number.
exercise: «Breathed-out air contains less oxygen and more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.» In this sentence, less means what? | Warmer | A bigger amount | Faster | *A smaller amount
exercise: In maths, what is ten less two? | 2 | 12 | 10 | *8
exercise: «Asking what will happen first makes it less strange.» What does less mean here? | Sooner | *Not so much | Lost | A bigger amount
test: «5 is less than 8.» Which sign shows this? | 8 < 5 | 5 = 8 | 5 > 8 | *5 < 8
test: «People blink less when they stare at a screen.» What does blink less mean? | Look at the screen all day | Stop breathing | *Blink not as often | Blink more often
exam: Which use of less means minus? | *Ten less two is eight | Less sugar in the tea | Five is less than eight | Asking less makes it strange
